Input, Output and String Manipulation in Python
1. Input in Python
Input means taking data from the user. Python uses the input() function.
Syntax:
variable = input("Enter value: ")
Example:
name = input("Enter your name: ")
print("Hello", name)
Output:
Enter your name: Preethi
Hello Preethi
Note: input() always returns data as a string.
Taking Integer Input
age = int(input("Enter your age: "))
print("Age:", age)
Taking Float Input
salary = float(input("Enter salary: "))
print("Salary:", salary)
2. Output in Python
Output means displaying information to the screen using the print() function.
Syntax:
print(value)
Example 1
print("Welcome to Python")
Output:
Welcome to Python
Example 2
name = "Preethi"
age = 20

print("Name:", name)
print("Age:", age)
Output:
Name: Preethi
Age: 20
3. String Manipulation in Python
A string is a sequence of characters enclosed in single (' '), double (" "), or triple (''' ''') quotes.
Example
name = "Python"
print(name)
Common String Operations
1. Concatenation (+)
Combines two strings.
first = "Hello"
second = "World"

result = first + " " + second
print(result)
Output:
Hello World
2. Repetition (*)
Repeats a string.
text = "Hi "
print(text * 3)
Output:
Hi Hi Hi
3. Length of String
text = "Python"
print(len(text))
Output:
6
4. Accessing Characters (Indexing)
text = "Python"

print(text[0])
print(text[3])
Output:
P
h
5. Slicing
text = "Programming"

print(text[0:6])
print(text[3:8])
print(text[-3:])
Output:
Progra
gramm
ing
Important String Methods
Uppercase
text = "python"
print(text.upper())
Output:
PYTHON
Lowercase
text = "PYTHON"
print(text.lower())
Output:
python
Capitalize
text = "python programming"
print(text.capitalize())
Output:
Python programming
Title
text = "python programming"
print(text.title())
Output:
Python Programming
Replace
text = "I like Java"
print(text.replace("Java", "Python"))
Output:
I like Python
Find
text = "Programming"
print(text.find("gram"))
Output:
3
Count
text = "banana"
print(text.count("a"))
Output:
3
Strip
text = "  Python  "
print(text.strip())
Output:
Python
Split
text = "Python Java C++"
print(text.split())
Output:
['Python', 'Java', 'C++']
Join
words = ["Python", "Java", "C++"]
print("-".join(words))
Output:
Python-Java-C++
Complete Example Program
name = input("Enter your name: ")

print("Original Name:", name)
print("Upper:", name.upper())
print("Lower:", name.lower())
print("Length:", len(name))
print("First Character:", name[0])
print("Last Character:", name[-1])
Sample Output
Enter your name: Preethi

Original Name: Preethi
Upper: PREETHI
Lower: preethi
Length: 7
First Character: P
Last Character: i
